Subject: Analyzing data from clustered camera traps with spatial mark-resight models
Message-ID: <EqnmLJoRtoQ.qmIDtZWM-1cJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/secrgroup/c/EqnmLJoRtoQ/m/qmIDtZWM-1cJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I am writing to get feedback on whether a clustered design for cameras rather than a uniform grid poses any problems in analysis of data with spatial mark-resight models models. Can anyone provide me with insights on this?   I am considering a clustered design (for a study of cats) because this appears to be more feasible logistically than a uniform grid and also may allow me to place more cameras in better locations (i.e., where there is a higher probability of obtaining photographs).  Thanks for any help.

From u118cea91a1619106 at groups.google.com  Fri May 29 21:08:26 2015
From: u118cea91a1619106 at groups.google.com (Murray Efford)
